      "math_academy_id": "q-178151",
      "sequence_position": 16,
      "problem": "$$\n{{N\\cap Z=N}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{3\\text{ is even}}}\\,\\overset{∨}{\\overset{⏞}{\\text{or}}}\\,\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{39\\text{ is prime}}}}_{⏟}}_{Q\\,∨\\,R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $Q∨R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $P∧(Q∨R)$ is {{field-3}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is true, $Q$ is false, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $Q∨R$ is false, and the result is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∧(Q∨R) & ≡\\text{true}∧\\overset{\\text{false}}{\\overset{⏞}{(\\text{false}∨\\text{false})}} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}∧\\text{false} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
